# CODEOWNERS — human-review gate for genuine risk paths.
#
# Why this exists: autonomous routines and the operating agent open PRs against
# this PUBLIC repo and merge them once CI is green and the linked issue is
# `spec-approved`. `main` requires no approving review in the general case. Any
# path listed below is the exception: it needs an approving review from a code
# owner before merge, regardless of CI. Enforced by the `main-protection`
# ruleset rule `require_code_owner_review`, which applies per path and to
# non-owner identities (verified 2026-09-22).
#
# Scope decided by the owner on 2026-09-22: gate identity/crypto, money,
# production schema changes, production deploy configuration and the merge gate
# itself. Everything else — routes, views, API surface, analyzers, scoring,
# tests, docs, internal metrics and refactors — is un-gated so it can merge
# autonomously. CODEOWNERS uses last-match-wins, so the broad un-gated
# directories simply have no entry here.

# The gate itself. Without this, a PR could remove every rule below.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @schmug

# Production deploy and release machinery: applies migrations, deploys Workers,
# cuts releases, rolls back, and decides which PRs are provenance-trusted.
/.github/workflows/migrate.yml          @schmug
/.github/workflows/deploy-mta-sts.yml   @schmug
/.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml   @schmug
/.github/workflows/release.yml          @schmug
/.github/workflows/rollback.yml         @schmug
/.github/workflows/pr-provenance.yml    @schmug
/.github/workflows/factory.yml          @schmug

# Production Worker configuration: routes, zone binding, D1/KV bindings.
# An `[env.*]` block here once detached dmarc.mx from its zone (#203–#206).
/wrangler.toml                          @schmug

# Identity, crypto/JWT, money, and self-serve erasure.
/src/auth/                              @schmug
/src/account/                           @schmug
/src/billing/                           @schmug
/src/webhooks/                          @schmug

# Production database shape. Migrations are applied to the live D1 database by
# migrate.yml and are effectively irreversible.
/src/db/migrations/                     @schmug
/src/db/schema.sql                      @schmug

# Retained beyond the categories above, for review by the owner:
# dependency supply chain (a lockfile change runs arbitrary code in CI),
# the gate script that authorises autonomous merges, the separately deployed
# MTA-STS Worker, and the written security policy.
/package.json                           @schmug
/package-lock.json                      @schmug
/scripts/routine-gate/                  @schmug
/mta-sts-worker/                        @schmug
/SECURITY.md                            @schmug
